Chapter: ShiftRange

  cites Foreword chapter Console

 COMPILER-158 (Damian, 2026-11-01): a shift count of 64 or more answers 0 for
 bit-shl and bit-shru and the sign fill for bit-shr; counts 0 to 63 are the
 ordinary shift. Each count arrives both as a literal and through a function
 argument, which the compiler cannot see as a constant.

Section: Helpers

  shl : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  shl (v) (n) = bit-shl v n

  shr : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  shr (v) (n) = bit-shr v n

  shru : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  shru (v) (n) = bit-shru v n

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("computed shl 1: 0=" & show (shl 1 0) & " 63=" & show (shl 1 63) & " 64=" & show (shl 1 64) & " 65=" & show (shl 1 65) & " 1000=" & show (shl 1 1000))
    print-line-uni ("computed shru 256: 8=" & show (shru 256 8) & " 63=" & show (shru (0 - 1) 63) & " 64=" & show (shru 256 64) & " 72=" & show (shru 256 72))
    print-line-uni ("computed shr: -256 by 4=" & show (shr (0 - 256) 4) & " -256 by 64=" & show (shr (0 - 256) 64) & " 256 by 64=" & show (shr 256 64) & " -1 by 100=" & show (shr (0 - 1) 100))
    print-line-uni ("literal: shl 1 64=" & show (bit-shl 1 64) & " shru 256 72=" & show (bit-shru 256 72) & " shr -256 64=" & show (bit-shr (0 - 256) 64) & " shl 3 2=" & show (bit-shl 3 2))
  end
